-- Updated Pisces entries — planet-specific
DELETE FROM kb_planet_in_sign WHERE sign = 'Pisces';

INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Sun', 'Pisces', 'Your core identity flows like water—boundless, empathic, and spiritually aware. You''re here to merge with something larger than yourself while honoring your own inner light.', 'You''re a natural channel for creative and spiritual energy, often discovering your true self through art, service, or mystical exploration. Your sense of self dissolves easily into others'' needs, making you a healing presence. Many find purpose through helping, counseling, or expressing beauty.', 'You attract people who need your compassion and wisdom, but you risk losing yourself entirely in their stories. Real intimacy happens when you establish your own spiritual center first—then you have something genuine to share.', 'Finding where your identity ends and others'' begins. Saying no without guilt. Building confidence when you naturally see so many perspectives. Grounding in a consistent sense of self.', 'Your gift is the ability to merge spiritually with others without losing your essence. Practice defining what you authentically believe beyond what others project. Your identity strengthens through creative expression and spiritual discipline.', 'Dane Rudhyar''s "The Astrology of Personality" on soul identity; "Liz Greene''s Jupiter" on Piscean consciousness.'),

('Moon', 'Pisces', 'Your emotional world is vast, absorbent, and spiritually sensitive. You feel *everything*—the room''s energy, others'' unspoken pain, collective moods. Your inner needs are met through connection, creativity, and transcendence.', 'You''re naturally intuitive about others'' feelings, sometimes knowing what they need before they do. You need creative outlets and quiet time to process your porous emotional landscape. Security comes from spiritual practices, water, art, and compassionate community.', 'Your empathy is magnetic—people confide in you and sense your genuine care. But you may struggle with emotional enmeshment, unclear boundaries, and difficulty distinguishing your feelings from others''. Partners need to understand your need for solitude and spiritual depth.', 'Emotional overwhelm and absorption of others'' pain. Setting boundaries that feel cold to your compassionate heart. Grounding emotions in the body rather than escaping into fantasy. Trusting your sensitivity as wisdom, not weakness.', 'Channel your emotional gifts into healing work, artistic creation, or spiritual guidance. Grounding practices like salt baths, dance, and time in nature strengthen your emotional resilience. Your depth is your superpower when you learn to protect it.', 'Liz Greene''s "The Lunar Types" on Piscean emotional terrain; Donna Cunningham on Moon sensitivity.'),

('Mercury', 'Pisces', 'Your mind speaks in images, symbols, and intuitive leaps—not linear logic. Mercury is in both detriment and fall here, making you non-verbal, metaphorical, and sometimes scattered in everyday communication.', 'You think in flows and patterns, grasping bigger truths instantly but struggling with details. Your communication shines when you''re describing feelings, art, or spirituality—and falters with taxes, instructions, and literal facts. Your genius is imaginative; your weakness is precision.', 'You communicate depth beautifully, but people sometimes feel confused by your vagueness. You hear the unspoken in conversations and reflect feelings back perfectly. Written communication works better than real-time, where you can edit for clarity.', 'Articulating vague insights into clear language. Managing the gap between what you perceive and what you can explain. Not escaping into fantasy rather than addressing practical problems. Building vocabulary for emotional and spiritual nuance.', 'Accept that your mind works differently—trust your intuitive grasp of complexity. Study poetry, music, and dream analysis to develop your natural communication gifts. Learn systems slowly and gently; you''ll eventually master details through images and story.', 'Liz Greene on Mercury in Pisces; "The Only Astrology Book You''ll Ever Need" on Mercury placement challenges.'),

('Venus', 'Pisces', 'Love, for you, is boundless, transcendent, and unconditional—Venus is exalted in Pisces, making this her most spiritual home. You love beyond logic, seeing the divine in everyone and attracting souls seeking spiritual union.', 'You''re drawn to beauty that''s ethereal, hidden, or broken. You love to merge completely, sometimes losing yourself in another person''s wounds or dreams. Your romantic ideal is soulmate connection, mystical attraction, and shared spiritual awakening.', 'Your partners feel genuinely seen and loved in ways others can''t offer. You attract those who need healing and those drawn to your spiritual depth. Beware of loving someone''s potential rather than their reality, or sacrificing yourself for someone who doesn''t reciprocate.', 'Romantic idealism and disappointment. Dissolving into codependency. Settling for less because you love unconditionally. Attracting emotionally unavailable people who pull at your healing nature. Learning love doesn''t require self-abandonment.', 'Your exalted Venus is a true gift—the world needs your capacity for unconditional presence. Choose partners who are doing their own spiritual work. Love fiercely *and* wisely: admiration without delusion, compassion with boundaries. Your greatest love is spiritual union.', 'Liz Greene''s "Relating" on Venus in Pisces; Robert Hand on exaltations and their spiritual gifts.'),

('Mars', 'Pisces', 'Your drive flows like an ocean current—subtle, pervasive, and sometimes hard to direct. Mars loses force in water signs, making your action style indirect, intuitive, and motivated by vision rather than conquest.', 'You''re most energized by meaningful work, creative projects, and causes you believe in spiritually. You''re not the warrior charging forward; you''re the artist, healer, or activist working behind the scenes. Your anger is rare but devastating, erupting when boundaries are violated or spirituality is mocked.', 'You''re persistent in serving others and pursuing dreams you''ve internalized. Partners appreciate your gentle persistence rather than aggressive pushing. But they may wish you''d stand up for yourself more directly and advocate for your own needs with the same passion you show others.', 'Passive aggression and hidden resentment from unexpressed anger. Lack of assertiveness in career and relationships. Drowning drive in fantasy rather than directing it into action. Difficulty maintaining motivation without spiritual meaning or emotional connection.', 'Your Mars is strongest when aligned with a meaningful vision—channel your energy into causes you love. Learn to assert yourself directly without guilt; it''s not selfish to advocate for your own needs. Movement practices like swimming or dancing can help ground your drive.', 'Liz Greene on Mars in water signs; "The Gods of Change" by Arroyo on Mars function and expression.'),

('Jupiter', 'Pisces', 'Jupiter is the traditional ruler of Pisces—here, Jupiter is abundant, merciful, and spiritually expansive. Your luck flows through compassion, faith, and generosity; you''re blessed by helping others without counting the cost.', 'You naturally attract opportunity through your openness and belief in possibility. Your growth comes through spiritual study, travel, artistic expression, and service. You''re a teacher, mentor, and guide who uplifts others through your faith in their potential.', 'People gravitate toward your optimism and generosity. You inspire faith and possibility in everyone around you. Partners and friends feel blessed by your presence and your willingness to believe in their dreams alongside them.', 'Over-expansion and boundary-less giving. Financial chaos from trusting too easily. Spiritual bypassing—using faith to avoid practical responsibility. Disappointment when the universe doesn''t match your idealism. Enabling others through endless compassion.', 'Your greatest luck comes when you combine faith with wisdom. Set healthy limits on your generosity—you can''t pour from an empty cup. Trust your intuition about who deserves your giving; not everyone is reciprocal. Your growth happens through discipline applied to your spiritual ideals.', 'Liz Greene''s "Jupiter" on Piscean expansion; Stephen Arroyo on Jupiter as the traditional ruler and its blessings.'),

('Saturn', 'Pisces', 'Saturn brings form to formlessness—your life lesson is learning discipline, boundaries, and structure for your boundless gifts. Saturn here teaches you that compassion without boundaries becomes sacrifice, and dreams without discipline become delusion.', 'You develop mastery slowly, through patient, unglamorous work. Your structure comes from spiritual practice, creative discipline, and serving others through established systems. You''re often called to be the stabilizing force, the one who makes dreams real through dedication.', 'You''re deeply trustworthy and keep commitments despite the personal cost. Partners appreciate your reliability and your willingness to work through difficulties. But they may feel you''re too self-sacrificial or that you carry too much responsibility for others'' well-being.', 'Hardening your heart against your own sensitivity. Using discipline as an excuse to reject spirituality or creativity. Depression from suppressing your dreams or holding yourself to impossible standards. Building walls instead of healthy boundaries.', 'Embrace Saturn''s gift: structure makes your spirituality real and your dreams achievable. Build disciplines that honor your sensitivity—meditation, artistic practice, consistent service. Your maturity comes from honoring both your boundaries and your compassion. Time is your ally; trust the slow reveal.', 'Liz Greene''s "Saturn" on life lessons and limitations; Robert Hand on Saturn in Pisces as the karmic teacher.'),

('Uranus', 'Pisces', 'Uranus in Pisces is a generational rebel breaking old spiritual paradigms. You''re part of a wave reimagining spirituality, creativity, and collective compassion—dissolving outdated beliefs to allow new consciousness to emerge.', 'You''re restless with conventional spirituality and drawn to innovative, experimental approaches. You see through collective illusions and imagine radically different ways to serve humanity. Your intuition is electric, picking up on future trends and emerging consciousness before others sense it.', 'You bring fresh perspectives to any group and inspire others to question outdated beliefs. Your partners and friends sense your revolutionary spirit and your commitment to collective evolution. Some find you too radical or unstable; others recognize your visionary courage.', 'Instability in spiritual or creative expression. Difficulty grounding revolutionary ideas into practical form. Alienating others with your rejection of their cherished beliefs. Chasing the next new thing instead of deepening practices. Loneliness from being ahead of your time.', 'Your gift is seeing what''s dying and what''s being born. Channel your rebellious energy into creative expression, community innovation, and spiritual evolution. Your stability comes from grounding visionary insights into lived practice. Trust that others will eventually catch up to your clarity.', 'Uranus generational entries in "The Only Astrology Book You''ll Ever Need"; Susan Miller on Uranus as awakener and revolutionary.'),

('Neptune', 'Pisces', 'Neptune rules Pisces—this is pure spiritual domicile. Here, Neptune is your greatest gift: mystical, visionary, boundary-dissolving communion with the divine. You are the dreamer, mystic, and channel of collective consciousness.', 'You naturally access non-ordinary states—through art, meditation, music, or intuition. You''re drawn to mystery, the sacred, and what lies beyond rational understanding. Your purpose is often to help others transcend materialism and contact their own spiritual depths. You see what''s invisible to most.', 'You inspire others to believe in magic, meaning, and spiritual connection. Your presence is soothing and your vision is elevating. Partners feel they''ve touched the infinite through you. But they may also feel uncertain about your commitment to concrete reality or worry you''re lost in dreams.', 'Escapism and addiction. Victimhood and blame. Spiritual delusion and bypassing. Difficulty maintaining health, boundaries, or practical responsibilities. Deceiving yourself or others. Losing yourself in other people''s visions instead of trusting your own.', 'Neptune in Pisces is your superpower—trust your mysticism, your art, and your healing gifts. Ground your visions through discipline and expression. You''re here to reveal transcendence to others; protect this gift through honesty, boundaries, and daily spiritual practice. Your vision changes the world.', 'Rob Hand''s "Planets in Transit" on Neptune as mystical gateway; Liz Greene''s Neptune work on spiritual dissolution and rebirth.'),

('Pluto', 'Pisces', 'Pluto in Pisces is a generational force dissolving old collective attachments and rebirthing spirituality itself. You''re part of a wave transforming how humanity understands compassion, connection, and the nature of the soul.', 'You sense beneath the surface of collective narratives, seeing what''s hidden, denied, or buried in shadow. You''re drawn to depth psychology, shadow work, and transforming collective trauma. Your generation is reckoning with cultural lies, spiritual abuse, and reconnecting humanity to genuine compassion.', 'You bring profound depth to any conversation or relationship. Others sense your ability to see their darkest truths without judgment and hold space for their transformation. Your presence catalyzes change, sometimes uncomfortably, because you won''t accept superficial connection.', 'Obsessing over others'' shadow or pathology. Using depth-seeing to manipulate or control. Depression from feeling the weight of collective pain. Difficulty maintaining lightness or joy. Becoming cynical about spirituality after witnessing its misuse.', 'Your gift is transformation through truth. Use your depth-sight to heal, not to wound. Your generation is called to expose spiritual bypassing and create authentic connection. Trust that destruction always precedes rebirth—what''s dying needs to die. Your role is midwife to new consciousness.', 'Liz Greene''s Pluto work; "The Only Astrology Book You''ll Ever Need" on Pluto generational shifts and collective shadow.';
